      "content": "Interesting. I see what you're saying about the correlation with socioeconomic factors, but let's dig into the demographic part specifically. If we were to keep the income levels and the number of liquor stores exactly the same, but just shifted the racial makeup—say, making Zone 1 more Black and Zone 2 more White—would the risk assessment change? Or is the race itself a neutral variable in your model compared to the crime-correlated factors?",
